  "limitations": [
    "Binaries target Android API 24 in ARM64 and ARMv7, and run on newer connected Android versions; no real Android 7/API 24 phone has been connected",
    "ARMv7 Vulkan 1.0 and explicit 1.1 CPU/GPU transfers passed on RedMagic; Pixel reports only ARM64 and rejects explicit ARMv7",
    "A real Vulkan 1.0 memory survey on the same RedMagic GPU reports a 4-GiB heap in ARMv7 but an 11.58-billion-byte heap in ARM64; actual current-process properties must always be queried",
    "Vulkan 1.0 is really requested and used on physical GPUs reporting 1.1 and 1.4; a hardware Vulkan 1.0-only device has not been connected",
    "A native C mock verifies the Vulkan 1.0 loader with no vkEnumerateInstanceVersion and a Vulkan 1.0 physical device",
    "On Pixel, a real noncoherent HOST_VISIBLE staging type is allocated and real Vulkan 1.0 flush and invalidate return VK_SUCCESS around a verified GPU Compute workload",
    "On RedMagic, the exact staging-upload memoryTypeBits do not permit a noncoherent HOST_VISIBLE type, and the explicit test returns VK_ERROR_FEATURE_NOT_PRESENT without fallback",
    "The default mode prefers coherent staging memory where available; no phone vendor or model participates in runtime allocation selection",
    "Only a synthetic 32-bit integer SPIR-V 1.0 workload is tested, not a hashcat Vulkan backend or credential-processing workload",
    "The original Qualcomm OpenCL bcrypt self-test code 245 remains unresolved"
  ],
